{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Core-Plugins-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Plugins vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Core Plugins","anchor":"Core-Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Importing at call sites","level":3,"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}]},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice (","type":"text"},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"View","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to that file.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Comparison"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" to react to every dispatch","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add state, action case, and register","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"text":"The Decision Rule","level":2,"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the plugin need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", it’s a core plugin — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and handle its own actions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":". A domain plugin that must also react to every dispatch, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" do, adds "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins handle their own actions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"service-result action","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo plugin"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","kind":"article","title":"Security Posture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","role":"article","title":"Design Principles","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Persistence Plugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","kind":"symbol","title":"PluginHost","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}]}}}